---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/viswaroop-print-portrait.png';
import {getCollection} from 'astro:content';
const latest=(await getCollection('blog')).sort((a,b)=>b.data.date.valueOf()-a.data.date.valueOf())[0];
---
<Layout title="Home">
<div class="atlas-topline"><span>PERSONAL ATLAS / VISWAROOP VADLAMUDI</span><span>OPEN ENDED, BY DESIGN <span class="orange">↗</span></span></div>
<section class="atlas-intro" aria-labelledby="atlas-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Staff software engineer & a curious human</p><h1 id="atlas-title">VISWA<span>ROOP<span class="orange">.</span></span></h1><div class="intro-under"><span class="coordinate" aria-hidden="true">↳</span><p>Building platforms.<br/>Questioning boundaries.<br/>Making sense of things.</p></div></div><div class="intro-personal"><figure class="portrait-print portrait-home"><Image src={portrait} alt="Illustrated portrait of Viswaroop Vadlamudi, smiling in a white shirt" width={440} height={440} widths={[220,440]} sizes="220px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="eager" /></figure><p>I work on infrastructure and identity. But this space holds more than the job: the systems I’ve built, the books I’ve learned from, and the questions I’m still carrying.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Meet the person behind the diagrams ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="connection-map" aria-labelledby="map-title"><div class="map-legend"><h2 id="map-title">Nothing here exists in isolation.</h2><span class="eyebrow">Choose a thread ↓</span></div>
<div class="map-surface">
<svg class="map-wires" viewBox="0 0 1000 365" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M170 92H360V164H480M530 190V285H725M480 170H730V80H850M170 105V290H250M525 150V48H460"/><circle cx="480" cy="164" r="5"/><circle cx="360" cy="92" r="4"/><circle cx="730" cy="170" r="4"/></svg>
<a class="map-stop stop-work" href="/work/"><span class="map-id">01 / WHAT I BUILD</span><strong>Systems</strong><span>Clouds, identity, guardrails.</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
<a class="map-stop stop-writing" href="/blog/"><span class="map-id">02 / WHAT I NOTICE</span><strong>Field notes</strong><span>Lessons from real systems.</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
<a class="map-stop stop-now" href="/now/"><span class="map-id">04 / STILL UNRESOLVED</span><strong>Open questions</strong><span>Agents. Context. Authority.</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
<a class="map-stop stop-books" href="/tags/books/"><span class="map-id">03 / WHAT I TAKE WITH ME</span><strong>Books & ideas</strong><span>Fewer highlights. More application.</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
<p class="map-annotation">Good ideas tend<br/>to cross boundaries.</p>
</div><div class="map-foot"><span><span class="legend-square" aria-hidden="true"></span> A place to start</span><span><span class="legend-line" aria-hidden="true"></span> A connection worth following</span><span>NO SINGLE CORRECT PATH</span></div></section>
<section class="desk-notes" aria-label="Currently on my desk"><div class="desk-label"><span class="eyebrow">ON THE DESK</span><span class="desk-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↘</span></div><a href={`/blog/${latest.slug}/`} class="desk-entry"><span class="eyebrow">Latest note</span><h2>{latest.data.title}</h2><span class="tiny-link">Read the note ↗</span></a><a href="/blog/2026-01-06-books-to-read-in-2026/" class="desk-entry"><span class="eyebrow">On the reading list</span><h2>The Staff Engineer’s Path</h2><p>Tanya Reilly — influence without a management title.</p><span class="tiny-link">The reading list ↗</span></a></section>
<section class="atlas-signoff"><p>Have a question, a hard problem,<br/>or a good book recommendation?</p><a href="mailto:hello@viswaroop.dev">LET’S TALK <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</Layout>
